@startuml
title Public decryption: whitepaper flow vs implemented flow
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
  ActorBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ActorBorderColor #4A78B5
  LifeLineBorderColor #4A78B5
  ArrowColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F3F7FD
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
autonumber

participant "Contract" as C
participant "Oracle\n(whitepaper only)" as O
participant "Gateway" as G
participant "KMS" as K
actor "User / any caller" as U

== Whitepaper v3.1: oracle-based ==
C -> C : FHE.requestDecryption(cts, callbackSelector)
C --> O : DecryptionRequest event
O -> G : forward request
G -> G : ACL check on Gateway copy,\nciphertext material added?
G -> K : decryption event
K -> G : t + 1 signed plaintexts
G --> O : result event
O -> C : callback(requestID, plaintexts, signatures)
C -> C : FHE.checkSignatures(requestID, signatures)

== Repository: self-relaying ==
C -> C : FHE.makePubliclyDecryptable(handle)
U -> G : publicDecrypt(handle) via relayer SDK
G -> G : ciphertext material added?
G -> K : decryption event
K -> K : read host chain ACL:\nhandle publicly decryptable?
K -> G : t + 1 signed plaintexts
G --> U : cleartext, ABI encoding,\ndecryption proof
U -> C : submit(cleartext, proof)
C -> C : FHE.checkSignatures(handles,\nabiEncodedCleartexts, decryptionProof)
note over C, U #F3F7FD : No component is obliged to complete the second flow;\nthe contract must be designed for a reveal that may never arrive.
@enduml
